course: dictionary
lesson: 1543
title: The person who leads the meeting
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A chairman is the person who leads a meeting or a committee. They keep order, decide who speaks next, and stick to the plan for the meeting, called the agenda. Context helps: in school councils and clubs, the chair runs the meeting and lets everyone have a turn.
explain: Look at the clues in the story. «The Chairman of the Bench of Magistrates calls Toad the incorrigible rogue and hardened ruffian» and then asks how to punish him. Magistrates are judges of a local court, so the Chairman is the one leading the judges. Ask yourself: who is in charge here? That is the chairman.
explain: Another clue is «Order, order!», which the chairman calls out when people need to be quiet and listen. In stories, the chairman may bang a gavel, a small wooden hammer, to get attention. Today many people say chair or chairperson instead, so the word fits anyone.
fact: A chairman leads a meeting or committee and keeps order.
fact: A chairman can also be the person in charge of the board of a company, club or organisation.
fact: The plural of chairman is chairmen.
fact: Chair, chairperson and chairwoman can all mean the same person who leads.
fact: Chairperson is a good choice when you do not know, or do not want to say, whether the leader is a man or a woman.
exercise: «Make it a round twenty.» «Excellent!» says the Chairman. What is the Chairman's job in this part of the story? | *Leading the meeting and keeping order | Baking cakes for the court | Stopping the rain | Driving the coach to the town
exercise: Which word means the same as chairman, and fits anyone? | Judge | Toad | Gavel | *Chairperson
exercise: What is the plural of chairman? | *chairmen | chairmans | chairmanes | chairmens
test: What does the chairman decide during a meeting? | *Who speaks next | The colour of the walls | Which biscuits to eat | What the weather will be
test: Why might a chairman call out «Order, order!»? | To start a race | To wake up the sleeping judges | To ask for a cup of tea | *To ask everyone to be quiet and take turns
exam: In «The Chairman of the Bench of Magistrates calls Toad the incorrigible rogue», what does Chairman most likely mean? | *The person who leads the court and keeps order | A player in a game | A toad who is in charge of the river | A person who sells furniture
